  "prefLabel": "Fors 103.01 Duties and Responsibilities",
  "priorExpiration": "1998-02-05",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Fors 103.01 Duties and Responsibilities. The board shall administer the provisions of RSA 310-A:98-117 which include but are not limited to:\n\n(a) Establishing and maintaining a high standard of integrity, skills and practice in the profession of forestry;\n\n(b) Administering the application procedure for obtaining a license;\n\n(c) Evaluating qualifications of applicants;\n\n(d) Administering examination procedures;\n\n(e) Administering renewal procedures and continuing education requirements;\n\n(f) Establishing ethical and professional standards; and\n\n(g) Implement disciplinary actions.\n\nSource. #5222, eff 9-11-91; EXPIRED 9-11-97\n\nNew. #6597, INTERIM, eff 10-8-97, EXPIRED: 2-5-98\n\nNew. #6915, eff 12-22-98",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/fors100-500.html"
